mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Histology & Embryology is composed of both Histology and Embryology that are independent subjects but closely related to each other. Histology focuses on the study of micro- and ultra-structure of human body observed under light and electron microscope, and also on their relevant physiological functions. Embryology concentrates in the study of embryonic developmental process and relevant mechanisms by which birth defects occur.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
